"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 10 and positive surgical margins. The pathological findings show an ISUP grade group 1 (Gleason 3+2) with pT3a disease, which are concerning elements. Countervailing findings include no documented extraprostatic extension and that the seminal vesicles were not invaded. A significant limitation is the absence of nodal sampling; therefore, the current staging cannot definitively assign a node status. Furthermore, there is a discrepancy between the biopsy finding (Gleason 3+4) and the prostatectomy specimen grade (Gleason 3+2). The prognosis would be significantly revised by obtaining postoperative PSA levels and tracking their subsequent trajectory over time. The fixed estimated horizon is 69.39 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 41.64–97.15 months; its coverage has not been validated."
